  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There are a literally TON of maps in VRChat that users have created and have existed for a very long time. But what about worlds that basically don't do anything and is just a waste of space for VRChat to hold on their serves? \nLet's say that a world from years ago using SDK2 that was only used to test something small and could be broken by now still exists. We don't need worlds like this as it just takes up space on VRChats side.\nSo what if there was a review that they would carry out to see if it's worth deleting or not unless it gets updated. VRChat could email the user addressing the world status and could provide some sort of check-list to give to the user if they wish to keep their map on VRChat or not.\nI feel like nowadays we are making huge worlds and some of them don't even get used or just too old and/or broken to be kept on their servers. I know this is just a stupid idea that I honestly just thought about and I don't expect this to do well... Just saying that maybe it would be good to be out with the old and in with the new.",
